<task id="169" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Mirror task 156's IntermediateRootColumns in the TypeScript stamp derivation (PolymorphicResolverService.deriveCoreAncestorStamps): a child picked in the RegardingResolver PCF under an invoice, document, budget or report card is stamped with that record's root at save time, two different roots of one type refuse, and C# lock-step tests keep the TypeScript tables equal to the server's</title>
    <phase>Session 27 — UAC defect remediation (task 156 follow-up, item 13a; owner round 8)</phase>
    <gate>startable after task 156 is merged into work/unified-access-control-r2 (at authoring it is NOT merged: branch task/uac-r2-156-r1-r2b @ a827ea0dc)</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes the FR-26 access stamp the client writes on a child record. That stamp is the access edge: it decides which root's principals inherit the child and, through tasks 155/156, where its file bytes go. Modifies .ts and .cs files and tests (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-language parity of an access-control table; a behaviour change in a shared client library consumed by a deployed PCF; fail-closed decisions that change what a user can save.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Bumps the RegardingResolver PCF version and edits its tests; task 147 also edits RegardingResolver (`ResolverWriteHandler.ts`) and shared client packages, and bumps the same control's version. Edits `CoreAncestorResolverTests.cs` and doc comments in `CoreAncestorResolver.cs`, which task 156 owns until it merges. Serialize after 156; serialize with 147 on the RegardingResolver files and version. Touches no `Api/ExternalAccess/**` or `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**` file.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>156</deps>
    <tags>pcf, shared-lib, security, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Task 156 verifier round 2 item 13a (notes/task-156-stamp-freshness.md on task/uac-r2-156-r1-r2b: "Item 13a — not closed in this round, and why", and decision (xii)). Filed as work, not deferred, by owner round 8 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md, round 8: "156 item 13a: mirror IntermediateRootColumns in the TypeScript PolymorphicResolverService.deriveCoreAncestorStamps, with a C# lock-step test"). Owner rules that bind it: no deferral; ADR-003 fail closed; ADR-002 WP-2 (the server owns the invariant, the client previews it, and must not preview a different answer). Owner round 8 item 3 raises the stakes: the four `sprk_regarding{core}` columns are to become read-only on the to-do, event, communication and analysis forms, so the RegardingResolver picker becomes the only way a user sets a root.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Task 156 taught the server that a child's core-ancestor stamp is the root of WHATEVER it is filed under (communication, event, to-do, analysis, invoice, document, agreement, report card, budget), each read through its own root columns, and that two different roots of one type on one record are an error. The TypeScript twin used by the RegardingResolver PCF still reads only the four sprk_regarding{core} columns, and only for the six CHILD entities. Make the TypeScript derivation read exactly the same table with exactly the same ambiguity rule, prove it with jest, and add C# tests that fail the build when the TypeScript tables differ from the server's.</prompt>

  <amendments source="main session, 2026-10-03, owner rounds 9-10" binding="true">
    <!-- Read these before step 0. Each overrides anything below that contradicts it. -->
    <amendment>Owner decisions now run to round 10: re-read notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md rounds 9 and 10 on work/unified-access-control-r2 before step 0. They are newer than this POML.</amendment>
    <amendment>Task 156's final, verified branch is task/uac-r2-156-c1-r2 (ready to merge, not yet integrated). Build on it, not on task/uac-r2-156-r1-r2b.</amendment>
  </amendments>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: the shared client library @spaarke/ui-components (PolymorphicResolverService, ADR-012 / ADR-024), the RegardingResolver PCF, and the BFF unit tests that pin client/server parity.</role>

  <goal>After this task:
(1) `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts` exports a literal table `INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS` whose rows equal, as a set, the flattened C# `CoreAncestorResolver.IntermediateRootColumns` on the merged task 156 code (30 rows at authoring, listed in the background).
(2) `deriveCoreAncestorStamps` derives for every target that is an intermediate in that table, not only `CHILD_RECORD_ENTITIES`: one read of the target's own root columns that exist on it, each non-null value becoming a stamp on the CHILD's matching `sprk_regarding{core}` column (from `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS`), never on the intermediate's own column name.
(3) Two columns of one root type on the target naming DIFFERENT records return `status: 'error'` with no stamps (same rule as C# `ResolveStampsAsync`); the same record named twice gives one stamp.
(4) CORE targets, unclassified targets (`sprk_organization`, `contact`, `account`, anything not in the table) and every existing fail-closed branch behave exactly as today.
(5) `CORE_RECORD_ENTITIES`, `CHILD_RECORD_ENTITIES`, `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS`, `isCoreRecordEntity` and `isChildRecordEntity` are byte-for-byte unchanged (the access taxonomy does not move).
(6) Two new C# unit tests in `CoreAncestorResolverTests.cs`: `IntermediateRootColumns_MatchTheTypeScriptSide` parses the TypeScript table the way `Taxonomy_MatchesTheTypeScriptSide` parses the taxonomy arrays and fails on any difference; `CoreAncestorLookups_MatchTheTypeScriptSide` pins the root → stamp-column pairs of `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS` to C# `CoreAncestorLookups` (the mirror writes its stamps through that table, and today no test pins it across languages).
(7) The RegardingResolver PCF is version-bumped, built with `npm run build:prod`, its Solution folder carries the new bundle, and its deployment is recorded as a manual gate for the main session.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>WHY. Task 156 extended the SERVER derivation (`CoreAncestorResolver.IntermediateRootColumns`, `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs:129-176` on task/uac-r2-156-r1-r2b) so that a to-do filed under an invoice, a budget or a document is stamped from their TYPED root columns, and agreement / report card from their own `sprk_regardingmatter` / `sprk_regardingproject`. Before 156 those children were born unstamped. 156 left the CLIENT twin alone (156 note, decision (xii) and item 13a): `deriveCoreAncestorStamps` still gates on `isChildRecordEntity` and reads only the four `sprk_regarding{core}` columns. Consequences today for the RegardingResolver PCF, all fail-closed but wrong:
  (a) a to-do picked under an invoice or a document is saved with NO stamp. Invoice and document carry none of the four columns, so the client returns `no-ancestor`. The to-do inherits nothing, and its uploads refuse `container_ancestor_stale` until the re-stamp that refusal enqueues lands or the 5-minute job runs.
  (b) a to-do picked under a budget or a report card returns `unclassified` and is saved unstamped, with the same window.
  (c) a to-do picked under a document whose `sprk_matter` and `sprk_relatedmatter` name different matters is saved unstamped, while the server refuses to derive anything for it.
The client previews a different answer from the one the server owns (ADR-002 WP-2).
AGREEMENT is in the server table, so it is in the TypeScript table (parity), but no RegardingResolver path can target an agreement today: `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG` (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder.ts:75-138`, 12 targets) has no `sprk_agreement` entry, the manual pick only accepts catalog entries (`ResolverWriteHandler.ts:350-364`), and auto-detect uses the same allowed catalog (`RegardingResolverApp.tsx:895-898`, `:966`). Agreement is covered by jest and the lock-step only; it is not part of the manual gate.

THE SERVER RULE TO COPY (verified on task/uac-r2-156-r1-r2b @ a827ea0dc, which is not merged at authoring; re-read it on the merged work branch at Step 0, line numbers may move):
  • Table: `CoreAncestorResolver.cs:154-173` `IntermediateRootColumns` (public static, a case-insensitive dictionary). The four standard tables use `StandardRootColumns()` (`:175-176`) = the four `CoreAncestorLookups` (`:107-113`) as (column, root). `sprk_document` (`:166-169`) is a PROJECTION of `Spaarke.Dataverse.DocumentLinkFields.All` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs:283-316`, unchanged by 156) filtered to targets matter / project / work assignment; `sprk_relatedservicerequest` and the non-root links are excluded by that filter.
  • Derivation: `ResolveStampsAsync` (`:439-570`): core target → itself, no read (`:459-467`); not in the table → Unclassified (`:472-475`); only the root columns present on the target are read (`:494-506`, none present → NoAncestor); probe or read failure / no row → Error (`:479-528`); the loop at `:531-559` keys stamps by ROOT ENTITY, skips null/empty, and when a second column of the same root type names a DIFFERENT id returns Error with no stamps (`:543-553`); the same id → `continue` (one stamp).
  • Known, pre-existing difference that this task KEEPS: when the metadata read succeeds but returns an empty column set, C# answers NoAncestor; the TypeScript `discoverNavProps` cannot tell an empty answer from a failed one (it returns `[]` on both, `PolymorphicResolverService.ts:471-516`), so TypeScript answers `error` (`:1026-1037`). The TypeScript side is the stricter, fail-closed one. Do not "align" it by weakening it; record it in the task note.
  • C# tests already pinning the rule (same branch, `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolverTests.cs`): `TypedRootIntermediates_DeriveTheirRoot` `:305-324`, `AgreementAndReportCard_DeriveTheirRoot` `:326-341`, `TwoDifferentRootsOfOneType_FailClosed` `:343-357`.

THE 30 ROWS at authoring (intermediate | column on the intermediate | root entity). The merged C# table is authoritative; if it differs, follow it and record the difference in the note:
  sprk_communication, sprk_event, sprk_todo, sprk_analysis — each: sprk_regardingproject | sprk_project; sprk_regardingmatter | sprk_matter; sprk_regardingworkassignment | sprk_workassignment; sprk_regardingservicerequest | sprk_servicerequest (16 rows).
  sprk_invoice: sprk_project | sprk_project; sprk_matter | sprk_matter.
  sprk_document: sprk_matter | sprk_matter; sprk_relatedmatter | sprk_matter; sprk_project | sprk_project; sprk_relatedproject | sprk_project; sprk_workassignment | sprk_workassignment; sprk_relatedworkassignment | sprk_workassignment.
  sprk_agreement: sprk_regardingmatter | sprk_matter; sprk_regardingproject | sprk_project.
  sprk_reportcard: sprk_regardingmatter | sprk_matter; sprk_regardingproject | sprk_project.
  sprk_budget: sprk_matter | sprk_matter; sprk_project | sprk_project.

THE CLIENT CODE TO CHANGE (work branch; 156 does not touch src/client, so these hold on the merged branch too): `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts` — `cleanGuid` `:367-370`; `discoverNavProps` `:471-516` (all ManyToOne relationships of an entity, so typed lookups such as `sprk_document.sprk_relatedmatter` are visible to it; cached per entity; `[]` on failure); `CORE_RECORD_ENTITIES` `:832-837`; the `CHILD_RECORD_ENTITIES` NOTE `:845-850` and array `:852-859`; `isChildRecordEntity` `:867-869`; `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS` `:886-903` (the CHILD's stamp columns and entity sets, and part of the pre-clear set at `:1193-1196`); status JSDoc `:917-934`; the function's class table `:949-955`; `deriveCoreAncestorStamps` `:974-1098` (core branch `:986-1010`; the `isChildRecordEntity` gate to replace `:1012-1015`; nav-prop presence oracle `:1022-1024`; discovery-failed error `:1026-1037`; no applicable column `:1039-1047`; the `$select` read `:1049-1064`; no row `:1066-1074`; the stamp loop to rewrite `:1076-1087`); `buildRegardingSelectionPayload` `:1165-1237` (unchanged; it already fails closed on `error` at `:1177-1184`).

CONSUMERS. Runtime callers of `deriveCoreAncestorStamps | buildRegardingSelectionPayload | buildTodoRegardingUpdate` in src, excluding the library itself and tests (grep at authoring):
  • RegardingResolver PCF manual pick: `src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/RegardingResolver/handlers/ResolverWriteHandler.ts:378-402`. On `error` it writes NOTHING, stages nothing and returns `success: false` (the form shows the error). This is where rule (3) newly refuses a save.
  • RegardingResolver PCF subgrid auto-detect: `src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/RegardingResolver/RegardingResolverApp.tsx:1183-1210`. On `error` it logs and stages NO stamps; it never blocks the host save (FR-24). Keep that behaviour.
  • `buildTodoRegardingUpdate` (`TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder.ts:187-231`): throws on `error`. It is exported through the `services/index.ts` barrel (`:141-150`), but NO runtime caller exists in src at authoring.
  No other PCF, code page or add-in calls any of the three. Packages that BUNDLE the module without calling the derivation (grep for `PolymorphicResolverService|TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder` at authoring; Step 0 records the full list): the CommunicationConnections and VisualHost PCFs; the code pages EventDetailSidePane, SmartTodo, Notepad, NavigatorPane, SpaarkeAi and CommunicationPage; the shared packages Spaarke.Communication.Components and Spaarke.AI.Widgets, and the wizards inside Spaarke.UI.Components. Their behaviour does not change, so this task does not require their redeploy; they pick up the new table on their next routine rebuild.
  The PCF consumes the library through `file:../../shared/Spaarke.UI.Components` and deep `dist/` imports (`ResolverWriteHandler.ts:59-75`); its `prebuild:prod` runs `shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/scripts/ensure-dist-fresh.js`, which rebuilds the library's `dist/` when it is older than `src/`. Its jest maps `@spaarke/ui-components/dist/*` to the library SOURCE (`src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/jest.config.js`), so `ResolverWriteHandler.test.ts` exercises the real derivation, while `RegardingResolverApp.test.tsx` mocks it.

PCF VERSION, currently 1.5.0. The four locations of the `src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md` "Version Update Checklist": (1) `RegardingResolver/ControlManifest.Input.xml:3` `version="1.5.0"`; (2) the UI footer: `RegardingResolver/index.ts:32` `CONTROL_VERSION = '1.5.0'` plus `RegardingResolver/RegardingResolverApp.tsx:311` `BUILD_DATE`; (3) `Solution/solution.xml:11` `&lt;Version&gt;1.5.0&lt;/Version&gt;`; (4) `Solution/Controls/sprk_Spaarke.Controls.RegardingResolver/ControlManifest.xml:3` `version="1.5.0"`. Also `Solution/pack.ps1:1` `$version = "1.4.9"` is stale (it names the zip); set it to the new version.

EXISTING TESTS: jest `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/__tests__/PolymorphicResolverService.coreAncestor.test.ts` (fixtures `:45-172`, incl. `metadataFetchStub` `:104-127`, whose empty column list answers `ok` with no rows, i.e. the discovery-failed branch, and `buildWebApi` `:143-169`; taxonomy `:182-228`; derivation `:234-399`; builder `:401-579`). `__tests__/TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder.test.ts` stubs metadata with only the four `sprk_regarding{core}` columns for every entity (`:44-64`), so invoice / budget / document targets there resolve `no-ancestor` before and after this task. PCF `src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/__tests__/ResolverWriteHandler.test.ts` (`navRow` `:74-80`, `FULL_NAV_PROPS` `:100-115`, `makeFetch` `:147-157`, which answers 404 for an entity it has no rows for; the no-ancestor case `:395-414`). C# `Taxonomy_MatchesTheTypeScriptSide` (`CoreAncestorResolverTests.cs:126-145` on the 156 branch) with helpers `FindRepoFile` `:561-571` and `ParseTsStringArray` `:574-585` (regex over `export const NAME: ... = [ ... ]`, the body captured up to the first `]`, then every `'…'` literal).

PRETTIER (repo `.prettierrc`): printWidth 120, singleQuote, trailingComma es5. A row that formats past 120 characters is broken across lines with a trailing comma after its last property, so the C# row parser must accept any whitespace and line breaks between tokens and an optional trailing comma.

ADR-012 PATH A EXCEPTION. `notes/phase3-derivation-rules.md` §7 "ADR-012 tension 1" records a project-scoped §6.5 Path A exception for literal entity names, scoped to "the two taxonomy constants and `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS` … Nothing else." `INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS` is a new literal table of entity names, so it is outside that exception as written. The same rationale applies (an access-model table pinned by a test, not presentation), and the exception's scope must be widened explicitly, not silently.

LIVE FACT (156 note, 2026-10-02, read-only): 0 live `sprk_document` rows set any `sprk_related{matter,project,workassignment}` link, so rule (3) refuses no existing document today.

NO BFF ROUTE IS TOUCHED. The only `src/server` change is doc-comment text in `CoreAncestorResolver.cs`. `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests` (`tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs`, task 074, extended by task 167) is not affected: this task adds no route, fixes no route, and has no Pending waiver to delete, whether or not task 167 has landed on its branch.</background>
