  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the C# side. `CoreAncestorResolver.IntermediateRootColumns`, `CoreAncestorLookups`, `ResolveStampsAsync` and every other compiled C# member are NOT changed. The C# table is the source of truth; the TypeScript table follows it. The only `src/server` edit allowed is doc-comment text in `CoreAncestorResolver.cs` that describes the TypeScript side as deriving only the four columns.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the access taxonomy. `CORE_RECORD_ENTITIES`, `CHILD_RECORD_ENTITIES`, `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS`, `isCoreRecordEntity` and `isChildRecordEntity` are byte-for-byte unchanged, and `Taxonomy_MatchesTheTypeScriptSide` stays green unedited. Budget, report card and agreement become INTERMEDIATES (a child filed under them is stamped); they do NOT become CHILD entities. Do not add the new columns to `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS`: that list is the child's stamp columns and part of the pre-clear set of `buildRegardingSelectionPayload` (`:1193-1196`), and adding typed columns there would null a host's own `sprk_matter` / `sprk_project` lookups on every pick.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the table's shape. Declare `export const INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS` in `PolymorphicResolverService.ts` as a FLAT array of object literals, one row per (intermediate, column, root), every value a single-quoted string literal, in exactly this property order: `{ intermediate: 'sprk_document', column: 'sprk_relatedmatter', rootEntity: 'sprk_matter' }`. No spreads, no helper calls, no computed or referenced values, no nested arrays, and NO comments inside the array literal (group explanations go in the JSDoc above it), so the C# parser reads every row and nothing else. The type annotation contains no `=` (the existing parser's `:[^=]*=` relies on it). The derivation reads its rows ONLY from this array: any lookup structure it needs (rows by intermediate) is built from it in code, and no second list of root columns exists in TypeScript. Export it from the module only; the `src/services/index.ts` barrel is not changed (the PCF imports the module by deep path).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: `deriveCoreAncestorStamps`. Copy the C# rule exactly. Core target → unchanged (no read). Target not an intermediate in the table → `unclassified`, no read. Otherwise: the existing presence oracle (`discoverNavProps` of the TARGET; empty → `error`, unchanged), read only the target's root columns that exist on it (`$select=_{column}_value`, one read — ADR-034 one hop), none present → `no-ancestor`; read throws or returns no row → `error`. For each non-null value, the stamp is `{ entityType: rootEntity, entitySet and lookupAttribute from the CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS entry for rootEntity, recordId: cleanGuid(value) }`. A second column of the same root entity with a DIFFERENT id → `status: 'error'`, `stamps: []`, and an error text naming the target, the root type and both column names. The same id twice → one stamp. Zero stamps → `no-ancestor`. Ids are compared as `cleanGuid` values (braces and case removed), so `{ABC…}` and `abc…` are the same record. A root with no `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS` entry → `error` (unreachable while the closure test holds; fail closed rather than guess).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every new branch. Fail closed. An ambiguous target, an unreadable target row (including one the user has no Read on, which `Xrm.WebApi` returns as no row or as a thrown error), an unreadable metadata response or any exception produces `error` and no stamps: never a guess, never a partial stamp set, never a fallback to the four-column behaviour.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: consumers. Do not change how `ResolverWriteHandler.ts`, `RegardingResolverApp.tsx` or `TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder.ts` react to a status. Manual pick keeps refusing to write or stage on `error`; auto-detect keeps staging no stamps and never blocks the host save (FR-24); the builder keeps throwing. The only consumer-side edits are tests, the PCF version bump and `BUILD_DATE`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: whole task. No Dataverse plugin. The client stamp is a preview of the server-owned invariant (WP-2): the server table decides, the client copies it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012 / ADR-024 / CLAUDE.md §6.5">Scope: the shared library. `PolymorphicResolverService` stays context-agnostic (no `Xrm`, no PCF types); the derivation stays in the shared service and is not re-implemented in the PCF. `INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS` carries literal entity names: widen the Path A exception in `phase3-derivation-rules.md` §7 "ADR-012 tension 1" to name it explicitly, with the same rationale, and cite the widened exception in the PR for code-review approval. No other new literal entity-name table is added.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. jest goes through the existing `IPolymorphicWebApi` shim, and the existing `metadataFetchStub` (library) / `makeFetch` (PCF) for the metadata endpoint only (the library test file's own doctrine, `:17-20`); do not add a second fetch stub. No live Dataverse in any test or in CI.</constraint>
