  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS` is exported from `PolymorphicResolverService.ts` as a flat array of single-quoted object literals in the property order intermediate, column, rootEntity, with no spread, computed entry or comment inside the array; `src/services/index.ts` is unchanged; `deriveCoreAncestorStamps` reads root columns from no other list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">C# `CoreAncestorResolverTests.IntermediateRootColumns_MatchTheTypeScriptSide` passes. It locates the TypeScript file with `FindRepoFile` and finds the constant (failing with a message naming it if absent). It parses every row with a regex that accepts any whitespace or line breaks between tokens and an optional trailing comma. It fails if the array body contains `...`, `//` or `/*`, or if the number of `{` in the body differs from the number of parsed rows. It asserts the parsed rows equal the flattened C# `IntermediateRootColumns` as a set, compared in lower case, with equal counts and no duplicates.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">C# `CoreAncestorResolverTests.CoreAncestorLookups_MatchTheTypeScriptSide` passes: it parses the (entityType, lookupAttribute) pair of every row of the TypeScript `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS` and asserts they equal C# `CoreAncestorLookups` as a set with equal counts; it does not require any edit to `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Taxonomy_MatchesTheTypeScriptSide` passes unedited; `git diff` shows no change to `CORE_RECORD_ENTITIES`, `CHILD_RECORD_ENTITIES`, `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS`, `isCoreRecordEntity` or `isChildRecordEntity`, and no change to any compiled C# member (only comment lines differ in `CoreAncestorResolver.cs`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">jest, typed roots: an invoice target with `_sprk_matter_value` set, a budget target with `_sprk_project_value` set, and a document target with only `_sprk_relatedmatter_value` set each return `derived` with exactly one stamp whose `lookupAttribute` is the child's `sprk_regardingmatter` / `sprk_regardingproject` and whose `entitySet` comes from `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS` (never `sprk_relatedmatter` or `sprk_matter`). An invoice with both `_sprk_matter_value` and `_sprk_project_value` set returns two stamps, one per root type, as the server does.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">jest, agreement and report card: each with `_sprk_regardingproject_value` set returns `derived` with one project stamp, and `isChildRecordEntity` still returns false for both.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">jest, the read: for a document target the single ancestor read selects exactly the document root columns present in the metadata stub (and no `sprk_regarding{core}` column, no `sprk_relatedservicerequest`, no non-root link such as `sprk_invoice`); exactly one ancestor read happens per derivation (one hop).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">jest, negative (ambiguity): a document whose `sprk_matter` and `sprk_relatedmatter` name different matters returns `error` with `stamps: []`; so does one whose `sprk_project` and `sprk_relatedproject` differ; so does one whose `sprk_workassignment` and `sprk_relatedworkassignment` differ; `buildRegardingSelectionPayload` for the first returns `success: false` and no payload.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">jest, dedupe: a document whose `sprk_matter` and `sprk_relatedmatter` name the same matter, one braced and upper-case and one bare, returns `derived` with exactly one matter stamp.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">jest, negative (fail closed on a new intermediate), for a budget target: metadata discovery failing → `error`; the ancestor read throwing → `error`; the read returning no row (the user cannot read the record) → `error`; the metadata listing only non-root columns (for example `ownerid`, so the list is not empty) → `no-ancestor` with no ancestor read; both root columns present but null → `no-ancestor`. In every `error` case `stamps` is empty.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">jest, unchanged behaviour: a core target still returns `core-target` with no read, and a matter target never stamps its own project; `sprk_organization`, `contact` and `account` targets return `unclassified` with no read and no metadata call; every pre-existing test in the file passes unedited, or any edited expectation has a one-line reason in the task note (escalation trigger 5 applies).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">jest, table closure: every `CHILD_RECORD_ENTITIES` entry is an intermediate in `INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS`; no `CORE_RECORD_ENTITIES` entry is an intermediate; every `rootEntity` is in `CORE_RECORD_ENTITIES` and has a `CORE_ANCESTOR_LOOKUPS` entry; no (intermediate, column) pair appears twice.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PCF jest (`ResolverWriteHandler.test.ts`, real derivation through the source mapping): a manual pick of a budget target whose `_sprk_matter_value` is set, on an existing host to-do, writes a payload binding `sprk_RegardingMatter@odata.bind` to `/sprk_matters({id})`. A manual pick of a document whose two matter links differ returns `success: false` with `ancestorStatus: 'error'` and `webApi.updateRecord` is never called, both for an existing host (a host GUID) and for a new host (no GUID, nothing returned for staging).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`RegardingResolverApp.test.tsx`, `regardingPresave.test.ts` and `TodoRegardingUpdateBuilder.test.ts` pass (unedited, or edited per escalation trigger 5).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeds S1-S11 are recorded in the task note, each with the test(s) that failed under it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RegardingResolver version bumped in the four locations and `pack.ps1`, `BUILD_DATE` set to the build date; `npm run build:prod` succeeds; the Solution folder's `bundle.js` and `ControlManifest.xml` are the new build's; the shared library `npm run build` and `npm run lint` succeed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Suites, counts recorded in the task note: the two affected library jest files and the full library jest suite; the full RegardingResolver jest suite; the full BFF unit suite; NetArchTest; `tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests` and `tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests` in full. No new failure against the base commit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Docs: the I-1 row no longer says the TS stamp mirror (or the RegardingResolver path) derives only the four columns, and still names the client create paths that do not stamp at all as a gap; `phase3-derivation-rules.md` §2/§3 describe intermediates and the ambiguity rule, and §7 names `INTERMEDIATE_ROOT_COLUMNS` in the Path A exception scope; the 156 note marks decision (xii) and item 13a closed by task 169; the `CoreAncestorResolver.cs` remarks say the client mirror derives the same table and name both lock-step tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">MANUAL GATE (main session, dev, after the code merges and after task 156's BFF is deployed). Deploy the RegardingResolver PCF with `/pcf-deploy` (build:prod → pack → solution-ZIP import), hard refresh and confirm the footer shows the new version. As an existing non-admin test user (ask the owner for one if none fits, owner round 4 item 1), on a new to-do form pick through the RegardingResolver (1) an invoice filed under a matter M the user can read, (2) a budget under M, (3) a document whose `sprk_matter` is M; after each save confirm read-only that the to-do's `sprk_regardingmatter` equals M. (4) If an invoice form has a to-do subgrid, create a to-do from its "+ New" and confirm the same (auto-detect path); otherwise record that there is none. (5) After the next run of the 5-minute reconciliation job, confirm none of these to-dos was re-stamped (their `modifiedon` is unchanged): the client and the server agree. If owner round 8 item 3's form lock is deployed by then, run (1)-(3) on the locked form; if a stamp does not land there, STOP and report. Delete the probe to-dos and record the deletion. Redeploy list: the RegardingResolver PCF only. No code page, other PCF or BFF redeploy is required for this task (none calls the derivation, per the Step 0 grep; the BFF has no compiled change). Results recorded in the task-169 note, ids redacted to the first 8 characters.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Task 156 item 13a, filed as work by owner round 8. Behaviour changes a reviewer should expect: (a) budget and report card targets move from `unclassified` to derived, so a to-do picked under one now inherits that record's matter or project at save time, which is what the server already does within minutes since 156 (agreement too, but no RegardingResolver path can target an agreement today); (b) invoice and document targets now derive from their typed links; (c) a RegardingResolver manual pick under a document naming two different roots of one type now refuses, matching the server (0 such live rows on 2026-10-02 per the 156 note; re-checked by escalation trigger 1). The subgrid auto-detect path keeps saving without a stamp in that case, and the server holds the row as ambiguous. The access taxonomy (CORE / CHILD) does not move. No BFF route, waiver or RouteAuthorizationGuardTests entry is involved.</notes>

